WEBVTT

00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:30.630
Bye.

00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:00.640
-

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.260
All right, we got it right here.

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:44.040
Thanks, Mr.

00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:45.270
Thanks very much.

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.490
Well, here we are.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:11.620
Yeah, we're here, all right.

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:15.750
Mr. Jones, you are now in the great southwest.

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.390
You are in the land of the long prairie,

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:23.030
where the coyotes howl and the winds blow free.

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:28.530
Don't smell no different yet to me than to do back home.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.770
There must be something wrong with your smellers.

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:34.940
Out here, everything is different.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:39.150
The trees are different, the people are different, the houses are different.

00:02:39.150 --> 00:02:43.010
But do you know they've got cows out here that don't give no milk?

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.710
There's rivers out here that ain't got no water in them?

00:02:45.710 --> 00:02:50.490
And there's men out here that can ride anything with hair on it.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.810
Yes, sir, Mr. Jones.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:57.520
And out here, a man's a man, and the women are glad of it.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:00.000
But listen, noose, have you got any objection?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:30.000
you telling me where we are going? Not at all, Mr. Jones, not at all. Mr. Jones, we are now following the advice of one of the finest men in America, Mr. Horace Greeley. Mr. Greeley said, go west, young man, and do your best, then come back east and spend your grief. Say, how come I couldn't go back

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:34.160
ease and get my grease and come back south and hush my mouth.

00:03:37.430 --> 00:03:41.390
Boy, you are so dumb until you think Spironica Lake is some kind of a summer resort.

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:42.650
Now, that's news.

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.650
Ain't no use you get mad, because you know I was just joking.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.650
You know I know you got plenty of sense.

00:03:48.070 --> 00:03:53.260
Why, if it wasn't for your sense, we'd both be spending 11 months and 29 days in the pee

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:54.830
patch back in Memphis, Tennessee.

00:03:55.110 --> 00:03:55.670
Now, wouldn't we?

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.060
Well, uh...

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.000
Sure we would.

00:04:01.560 --> 00:04:05.230
And here you come gettin' mad every time I say anything.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:08.180
Oh, July, you know I wasn't mad at you.

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:09.890
I was thinkin', that's all.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:12.610
And I get thinkin' real hard.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:15.260
I get sort of ugly in the face, you know.

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:17.420
Well, anybody can see you a hard thinker

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:22.660
just by lookin' at you.

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.160
What was that?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.390
I said I'm doing some hard thinkin' myself.

00:04:27.390 --> 00:04:28.230
Oh.

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.000
In fact, I'm doing some

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.960
Pretty hard thinkers right now.

00:04:34.330 --> 00:04:36.430
What are you thinking so hard about?

00:04:36.970 --> 00:04:41.090
But I was thinking that we could take that two bits you got and buy some sardines and crackers.

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:41.950
What do you think?

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:48.150
Well, I don't know.

00:04:49.050 --> 00:04:52.130
I don't think we ought to go cold in hand for no sardines and crackers.

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:59.610
And owing to the fact that that two bits we got is the last button on Gable's coat, it might be a good idea.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:05.530
I know, but owing to the fact we ain't greased our gums since way yesterday morning.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:08.630
Can you think of a better way to spend that last quarter?

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:12.540
I don't know. You have to give me time to think.

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:21.940
Wait a minute.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:27.680
How do you do, young man?

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:28.720
How you doing, sir?

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:30.000
Nice day, isn't it?

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:32.760
Oh, yeah, yeah, very nice day, very nice day.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:38.410
My name is Whitney, Vanderbilt Whitney, and yours?

00:05:38.790 --> 00:05:40.550
My name is Jefferson, Jefferson Lee.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:42.020
Glad to know you, Mr. Whitney.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.680
Oh, and I'm glad to know you, too, Mr. Lee.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:45.000
Yes, very glad to know you.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:50.440
You know, it makes me very proud to see a young man like you in business.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:51.300
It certainly does.

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:57.150
You know, when I saw you over here, I told my contemporary, Mr. Green over there,

00:05:57.530 --> 00:06:00.000
I said, now there's a young man in the business that's going for you.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:09.230
places. But I only work here. And when I said that, you said which? I only work here. You

00:06:09.230 --> 00:06:17.270
mean you don't own this business? That's right. Oh, the proprietor's not in just now, but maybe

00:06:17.270 --> 00:06:22.950
I can help you. Well, Sonny, the only way you can help me is to direct me and my friend

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:30.000
over here where we can get a room. Well, now, let me see. I love money.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.000
We just got in town, and what we need is nothing, anything else.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.830
There's a place I need, too, but it must be not.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:43.210
You might be able to roam down to my girlfriend's and boy, too, and a spare.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.490
Ah, now, if you just...

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.410
For the address?

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:46.390
No, Levine.

00:06:46.390 --> 00:06:49.540
Oh, I almost forgot about that.

00:06:49.540 --> 00:06:52.540
I think I got a quarter right here in my pocket.

00:06:52.540 --> 00:06:55.360
I don't like to break big bills just to get a quarter.

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.360
We got plenty of change.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.550
Uh-oh, but, uh...

00:07:00.410 --> 00:07:02.670
Yeah, it is.

00:07:03.170 --> 00:07:03.700
Thank you.

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:04.820
I'll see you later.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:05.740
Good day, sir.

00:07:11.130 --> 00:07:14.610
At ease.

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:40.760
The machine gun company, our president accounted for.

00:07:41.880 --> 00:07:44.550
Still fighting World War I.

00:07:45.070 --> 00:07:46.830
Mo, I was dead dreaming.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:47.630
That's all.

00:07:48.320 --> 00:07:50.180
Yes, I know you was dreaming.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.410
That's all you ever do is dream.

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:55.570
It's a good thing you wasn't in World War II.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:58.030
You'd dream yourself to death.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:00.000
Everybody else?

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:07.170
that didn't go. Got four Fs. You got four Fs to a G. I don't know what the G was for,

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:15.960
unless it was for good for nothing. Samuel Holiday. That name fits you to a T. You've

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:22.640
